Quantization

    It's a hack/trick to use less memory and less decrease in precision.

    a.  When we work with Deep Neural Network, we have to deal with lots of the parameters, and all these
        Numbers/Parameters are in 16 bits / 32 bits. They have a lot precision.
    b.  There is a simplification that we can do like cutting down the memory by taking each of these number
        which are stored in 16 / 32 bits and store them with lower precision by using fewer bits and make up a number

    Let's take an Example:
        Dimmer switch of a light bulbs
        When rotate the switch the light will decrease or increase

        1. If the light has 16 or 32 modes/settings the rotation will be very smooth
        2. Now we reduce it to 8 or 4 modes/setting then the dimmer switch will become less smoother. It will start making
        sounds like click, click.

    That's what it's like to take all these Parameters (Dimmer switches) all over our Neural Network layers and reduce
    the precision down to 8 or 4 bits from 16 or 32 bits.

    AND DOING THAT IS KNOW AS QUANTIZATION.

    *   We can think it as a quantising; turn it into something which has a discrete possible values and we reducing the
    precision so that we can squeez more into less memory. We can take less memory and the calculation wil b/c
    much more simple.
    *   If we are moving from 16 bits -> 4 bits then we are reducing 4 times of calculations and so that saving 4 times
        memory

